<title>NORWAY: Saga says oil output normal at Snorre.</title>
<headline>Saga says oil output normal at Snorre.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Saga Petroleum ASA said on Monday crude output at the North Sea Snorre development was running normally at about 200,000 barrels per day.</p>
<p>Saga resumed production at Snorre on Friday following five-day unscheduled shutdown due to a power outage.</p>
<p>&quot;Everything is running normally. Production is normal,&quot; a spokesman for Saga told Reuters.</p>
<p>Oil from Snorre is piped to the Statfjord development for final processing, storage and loading into dedicated shuttle tankers.</p>
<p>--Tanya Pang, Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
</text>
